{"acceptance_criteria":"","actor":"","agent_state":"","assignee":"Joey Thometz","await_id":"","await_type":"","close_reason":"Not feasible with default settings. Nano FP8 at default utilization uses 110 GiB of 119 GiB available — only 9 GiB free, far less than Super's 70 GiB weights. Dual-model serving would require restarting Nano at --gpu-memory-utilization 0.35 (42 GiB) so Super can use the remaining 77 GiB. Feasible mathematically but risky for demo stability. Deferred in favor of freq cap approach (hackathon-foc).","closed_at":"2026-03-17T22:30:13Z","closed_by_session":"","compacted_at":null,"compacted_at_commit":null,"compaction_level":0,"content_hash":"87835f36c30b51651e103f9911f00a5c8d160495da359d0dc55533e8f9136e6a","created_at":"2026-03-17T22:21:42Z","created_by":"Joey Thometz","crystallizes":0,"defer_until":null,"description":"Test if both models fit in 119 GiB. Start Super on :8002 first (70 GiB), then start Nano on :8000 (32 GiB). Check nvidia-smi after both start. Expected: ~102 GiB used, ~17 GiB free for KV caches. Commands: Super: VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP4=0 VLLM_NVFP4_GEMM_BACKEND=marlin vllm serve nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B-NVFP4 --port 8002 --trust-remote-code --max-model-len 4096 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.60. Nano already on :8000. Check: gpuctl exec gb10-hackathon 'nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid,used_gpu_memory --format=csv'","design":"","due_at":null,"ephemeral":0,"estimated_minutes":null,"event_kind":"","external_ref":null,"hook_bead":"","id":"hackathon-0gk.1","is_template":0,"issue_type":"task","last_activity":null,"metadata":"{}","mol_type":"","no_history":0,"notes":"","original_size":null,"owner":"joey@neuralwatt.com","payload":"","pinned":0,"priority":1,"quality_score":null,"rig":"","role_bead":"","role_type":"","sender":"","source_repo":"","source_system":"","spec_id":"","status":"closed","target":"","timeout_ns":0,"title":"Validate memory: can Nano FP8 + Super 120B load simultaneously?","updated_at":"2026-03-17T22:30:13Z","waiters":"","wisp_type":"","work_type":""}
