{"acceptance_criteria":"","actor":"","agent_state":"","assignee":null,"await_id":"","await_type":"","close_reason":"Fixed: per-IP 10s cooldown in proxy.py _stream_proxy(). Confirmed count=1 via curl grep test.","closed_at":"2026-03-17T22:32:43Z","closed_by_session":"","compacted_at":null,"compacted_at_commit":null,"compaction_level":0,"content_hash":"1f77a6ddf9d95738a611620ef90d9ad48e2c213c741783285eaa120dbc4ca274","created_at":"2026-03-17T22:16:33Z","created_by":"Joey Thometz","crystallizes":0,"defer_until":null,"description":"Double receipt persists. The \u003e=10 token threshold fix (commit 4fcda26) didn't help — both of OpenClaw's two calls per message generate substantial responses. OpenClaw runs a multi-step agent loop: initial context/planning call + final response. Both get receipts injected. Better fix needed: either (a) per-IP cooldown (skip receipt if another request came from same IP within last 5s), or (b) only inject receipt on the LAST SSE stream within a short time window, or (c) investigate if OpenClaw's pre-call can be identified by request shape (no user messages, or system-only) and skip receipt for those.","design":"","due_at":null,"ephemeral":0,"estimated_minutes":null,"event_kind":"","external_ref":null,"hook_bead":"","id":"hackathon-pxn.1","is_template":0,"issue_type":"bug","last_activity":null,"metadata":"{}","mol_type":"","no_history":0,"notes":"","original_size":null,"owner":"joey@neuralwatt.com","payload":"","pinned":0,"priority":1,"quality_score":null,"rig":"","role_bead":"","role_type":"","sender":"","source_repo":"","source_system":"","spec_id":"","status":"closed","target":"","timeout_ns":0,"title":"Double energy receipt in WebChat responses","updated_at":"2026-03-17T22:32:43Z","waiters":"","wisp_type":"","work_type":""}
